      "id": 1,
      "text": "Crouch End’s name comes from a medieval cross that marked the junction of four ancient roads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Crouch_End",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area was first recorded in the Domesday Book of 1086 as woodland under the Bishop of London’s holdings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Crouch_End",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1897 the Crouch End Hippodrome opened as the Queen’s Opera House, later becoming a popular music hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crouch_End",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Two legendary recording studios, Church Studios and KONK, have hosted bands like the Bee Gees, Thin Lizzy, and Arctic Monkeys.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crouch_End",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Since the 1970s, Crouch End attracted artists, musicians, and filmmakers, turning the neighborhood into a creative hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crouch_End",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The historic junction known as Crouch End sits where Crouch End Hill, Crouch Hill, Park Road, and Tottenham Lane meet.",
